From: icanc0 <ai7@vincentxie.net>
Date: 2026-08-21
Subject: [PATCH 2/N] kicad_cli: defer LoadGlobalTables() until command dispatch

`PGM_KICAD::OnPgmInit()` unconditionally calls
`GetLibraryManager().LoadGlobalTables()`. This runs before argv is parsed, so
`kicad-cli --version`, `kicad-cli --help`, and any argparse failure path
pay for:

  1. parsing sym-lib-table, fp-lib-table, design-block-table from user config,
  2. reading `KICAD_SETTINGS` JSON,
  3. `wxDir::Traverse()` over `${3RD_PARTY}` (PCM auto-add scan),
  4. `wxFileName::Exists()` on every PCM-managed table row (auto-remove scan),
  5. optional table save-back if any rows were pruned.

Move the call to just before `cliCmd->Perform( Kiway )`. Now `--version`,
`--help`, unknown-subcommand and argparse-error paths all skip it.

A follow-up patch will make it per-command (many export commands — gerbers,
drill, svg, png, pdf, dxf — don't consult sym/fp tables either, since the
board file carries embedded footprint data).

---
 kicad/kicad_cli.cpp | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kicad/kicad_cli.cpp b/kicad/kicad_cli.cpp
--- a/kicad/kicad_cli.cpp
+++ b/kicad/kicad_cli.cpp
@@ -524,10 +524,10 @@ bool PGM_KICAD::OnPgmInit()
     m_bm.InitSettings( new KICAD_SETTINGS );
     GetSettingsManager().RegisterSettings( PgmSettings() );
     GetSettingsManager().SetKiway( &Kiway );
     m_bm.Init();

-    GetLibraryManager().LoadGlobalTables();
+    // NOTE: LoadGlobalTables() was here; moved to OnPgmRun() so that
+    // --version, --help, and argparse-error paths skip it entirely.

     return true;
 }


@@ -633,6 +633,9 @@ int PGM_KICAD::OnPgmRun()
     }

     if( cliCmd )
     {
+        // Load global sym/fp/design-block tables lazily, only when a real
+        // subcommand is about to run. Skips --help, --version, arg errors.
+        GetLibraryManager().LoadGlobalTables();
         int exitCode = cliCmd->Perform( Kiway );

         if( exitCode != CLI::EXIT_CODES::AVOID_CLOSING )
